    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (87.42) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) as the clear engines of the offense. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.445 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Barnett, compounded by a significant park factor boost. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a high-priority start; despite a slight wind-in penalty, his dynamic platoon edge and status as a leadoff hitter make him essential for chasing those scarce stolen base points. **Lars Nootbaar** also grades out as a strong play (67.77) thanks to a massive 14% park boost and a high-leverage leadoff spot against Gordon, T.\n\nThe most difficult lineup decision today involved **Junior Caminero** (57.32) and **Carson Benge** (56.34), both of whom are startable but face non-ideal matchups. **Junior Caminero** was ultimately slotted into the UTIL spot despite a -19% penalty for facing Schlittler\u2019s elite-level xERA of 2.93, as his underlying power metrics maintained his floor above the margin. We continue to monitor **Caleb Durbin** (44.39); while his speed is an asset, he barely avoids the bench today because of the daunting 2.74 xERA of Espino. We are exercising caution with **Gary Sanchez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Hector Rodriguez**, all of whom reside in the marginal 50-53 point range; they provide enough value to hold their spots, but represent the first candidates to be pulled if we need to preserve game caps later in the week.\n\nWe are operating without **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** due to schedule conflicts, while **Colt Keith** remains sidelined on the IL. Our depth remains supported by **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**, though none challenged for a spot in today's high-ceiling configuration. Watch the weather reports specifically for **Pedro Ramirez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; the wind-in warnings at their respective venues have already tempered their output projections, and any further degradation in hitting conditions could push these players into \"below floor\" territory.",
